TKE can be produced by fluid shear, friction or buoyancy, or through external forcing at low-frequency eddy scales (integral scale). Turbulence kinetic energy is then transferred down the turbulence energy cascade, and is dissipated by viscous forces at the Kolmogorov scale. This process of production, transport and dissipation can be expressed as: D k D t + ∇ ⋅ T ′ = P − ε, where: D k D t is the mean-flow material derivative of TKE;
∇ · T′ is the turbulence transport of TKE;
P is the production of TKE, and
ε is the TKE dissipation.
